# SELVEDGE fail-closed refusal probes
# stamp: 20261114T184422Z
# revision: ff54b1f3117e3567039c7adc44e2d6fe63e87bcb
# host: Linux 7.3.3-1-cachyos x86_64
# Each case sets one limit to an invalid value and expects exit 78 with no container run.

=== CASE: SELVEDGE_MEM empty
command: env SELVEDGE_MEM= ./scripts/docker-court.sh rust -- cargo --version
court: SELVEDGE_MEM is empty; refusing to run without a hard limit
exit: 78

=== CASE: SELVEDGE_MEM zero
command: env SELVEDGE_MEM=0g ./scripts/docker-court.sh rust -- cargo --version
court: SELVEDGE_MEM='0g' is not a valid limit (must match ^[1-9][0-9]*[kKmMgG]$); refusing to run unbounded
exit: 78

=== CASE: SELVEDGE_MEM no unit suffix
command: env SELVEDGE_MEM=8192 ./scripts/docker-court.sh rust -- cargo --version
court: SELVEDGE_MEM='8192' is not a valid limit (must match ^[1-9][0-9]*[kKmMgG]$); refusing to run unbounded
exit: 78

=== CASE: SELVEDGE_MEM non-numeric
command: env SELVEDGE_MEM=lots ./scripts/docker-court.sh rust -- cargo --version
court: SELVEDGE_MEM='lots' is not a valid limit (must match ^[1-9][0-9]*[kKmMgG]$); refusing to run unbounded
exit: 78

